1. **PRIOR-WORK CHECK, before the first git write in your clone.** Read whole: RD-899 by Jira GET (`/rest/api/3/issue/RD-899?fields=summary,status,description,comment`; any JQL starts `project = RD AND ( ... )` WITH the parentheses; use NexusAI's read module: read `/Volumes/Laptop-DEV/!CODING/Datasec/NexusAI/session-tools/b774/b774lib.py` whole, load it with `python3 -I` through `importlib`, call only `get`, `search` and `adf_texts`; write verbs NOT yours); RD-894 (the cells this extends), RD-891 (the fix) and RD-892 by the same read; a search `project = RD AND ( text ~ "\"B865-2\"" OR text ~ "\"GM11\"" OR text ~ "\"B865-4\"" )` (drafter: RD-899, RD-894, RD-892; if a ticket OTHER than RD-899 now covers the write-failure cell, STOP naming it); `/usr/bin/grep -n -i -E 'RD-899|RD-894|RD-891|C-190|C-68\b|C-209|C-57\b|C-89\b|C-224' '/Volumes/Laptop-DEV/!CODING/Datasec/NexusAI/1_Project_Definition/CLARIFICATIONS.md' | cut -c1-300` (control: `RD-zzz9` prints none) and read the hits on the counts rule, the landing rule and any RD-891/RD-894/RD-899 note (by line range; the Read tool refuses the file whole); the gate record `Briefs/2026-10-28_B865_STATUS.md` (findings B865-1, B865-2, B865-4, the mutant table lines 55-72, C4 preconditions, C6b descriptor reuse), the builder record `Briefs/2026-10-28_B855_STATUS.md` (the three cells, the descriptor-reuse lesson, the counts precedent), and `Briefs/2026-10-28_B875_STATUS.md` (the records seat that filed RD-899); in your clone `git --no-optional-locks log --format='%h %s' -8 -- __tests__/rd891-probe-name-race.test.js backend/jsonStorage.js`; the open PRs and `b8*`, `b9*`, `records/*` branches (any touching your paths => STARTABLE NO). **A READY FOR QA, PARTIAL or STOPPED without a PRIOR WORK section naming what you read and found is returned unread.** PRIOR WORK must say what the change PRESERVES, each with its measurement: the 11 existing jest tests (same names, same statuses, same `Tests:` baseline; removed lines exactly two, cell G's); `backend/` byte-identical (`bba3742b`, numstat empty); every neighbour's `Tests:` line; the counts file moves only `tests` and `_updated`; the demo-deploy hold untouched; no alert dismissed; B890's file untouched.
2. **No production, no demo, no hosted site, no HTTP to any hosted host, no `az`, no Kudu, no docker, no ssh other than git's `core.sshCommand`.** The only outbound traffic is `npm ci`/`npm rebuild`, `git fetch`/`git push`, GitHub GETs, Jira GETs. Never touch `CI_DEPLOY_ENABLED`, a secret, an environment or the Actions settings. GitHub's core limit is shared (5000 an hour): no tight loops (30 s polls). The cells start no server and bind no port; any instrument of your own binds only 127.0.0.1 inside 9760-9769. **The cells touch the filesystem only inside `mkdtemp` directories under `os.tmpdir()`; the shared fallback directory is guarded and never written.**
3. **No message to any human.** No mail, chat, PR comment. No person's name and no decision-card id in STATUS, comments or commit messages (say "the product owner"); no B-number in a commit message, an added line, a Jira or a PR text (the branch name carries it by design). **Jira is READ ONLY (zero writes);** transitions and records are the records seat's, after the landing.
4. **Never delete** (`rm`, `git branch -d/-D`, `--prune`, `update-ref -d`, `worktree remove/prune`, `gc`, `reset`, `clean`, `stash`, `checkout -- <file>`); quarantine to `session-tools/b889/_quarantine/`. Restore a mutated file by writing the saved original over it and proving equality by hash and numstat. Never rebase, amend, squash or force-push; once pushed a correction is a STOP for the coordinator. Never write in the shared checkout `2_Project_Files`. Never open another seat's tree, kit or `session-tools/b[0-9][0-9][0-9]*` other than `b889` (finished seats' STATUS files and the Briefs evidence folders are read-allowed; B890's and B883's STATUS and trees are NOT yours to open).
5. **Shell:** never type `cd` (also not in a subshell or `npm ci` wrapper: use `npm --prefix <clone>` and `git -C`); absolute single-quoted paths (they contain `!`); read git with `--no-optional-locks`; `bash -c '...'` or a heredoc for chains; never an unquoted word starting with `=` (use `echo ----`); `/usr/bin/grep -i` with a positive control for every count; write `${VAR}:path`; STATUS and source files with the editor tool; never hand-edit `package-lock.json` or the counts file; never kill by basename (pid/port plus cwd); no `rm` of any kind, not even on `/dev/null` or a temp file; scratch goes under `session-tools/b889/`, not `/tmp`. Stop every process you start and record ports free again.
6. **Record every choice a reader would ask about** in STATUS under DESIGN with its source: **D1** why cell J goes into the EXISTING file (the ticket; the helpers it needs are that file's own and are not exported); **D2** why exactly one new cell (the counts figure is +1; B865-3 and B865-5 are held elsewhere); **D3** how J is made non-vacuous (its preconditions) and why green-at-main plus red-under-mutant is the proof here (no product defect to reproduce); **D4** what each mutant proved, with received figures; **D5** why G was widened with ENOSPC and not reworded (only the widening reddens GM6) and why the widening removes exactly two lines; **D6** why `--update-counts` ran once and the plain verify again at the final head (the pinned counts are the CI predicate); **D7** the placement of the new `describe` and whether J looped two codes; **D8** what you did NOT widen (the probe file's removal after a failed write, the mode, `isWritable`, the gate's other Notes).
