8. **Locks and load, by path.** The jest lock is the project's only jest mutex: `NEXUSAI_LOCK_BASE=/Volumes/Laptop-DEV/'!CODING'/Datasec/NexusAI/session-tools/locks-laptop-1017 bash /Volumes/Laptop-DEV/'!CODING'/Datasec/NexusAI/session-tools/nexusai-lock.sh jest b889-build-<step> <command>` (hash checked; usage from the tool's header `sed -n 1,40p`, never by invoking it to read it); FIFO; tag every ticket `b889-build-<step>`; `ls -la` of `queue-jest/` before and after each; never touch another seat's ticket, holder or tree; never `--replace` or `--after` a ticket that is not yours. Every jest run, mutant run and verify is a ticket. Hold limits: verify or `--update-counts` at most 35 minutes, any other ticket at most 20. **B890 (a storm file, heavy) and the gate B883 may hold the lock: WAIT, never refuse.** STOP only if the holder pid is gone while the directory still names it (report, never remove) or the holder's etime passes 150 minutes. If load1 stays at or above 7, wait (poll 30 s) and do light work meanwhile. Heartbeat per STATUS-NOW.
