10. **Landing is not yours and follows the project's rule** (`CLARIFICATIONS.md` C-190, line 2062, items 2 and 3 at lines 2067-2068 at the drafter's read: "Merge path: open a PR from the gated branch, wait for CodeQL (a background wait that EXITS), then land the SAME commit. Never squash, never rebase ([[C-68]])"; "NEVER dismiss a code-scanning alert, from any side, and never touch the ruleset"). The landing is a head-pinned MERGE commit of the gated head. The counts file's own `_why` says it IS the CI gate's expectation; your branch changes it only by the project's regeneration rule, once.

## STATUS-NOW (binding)
Write `/Volumes/Laptop-DEV/!CODING/Datasec/NexusAI/1_Project_Definition/Briefs/2026-10-29_B889_STATUS.md` at Step 0 and update it after every Step and jest hold. **Its FIRST line is the placeholder** `B889 STATUS (placeholder, Step 0 running)`, replaced by the real title when Step 0 completes. It holds the Step-0 block (sha256s of source and copy, slot count with control, REFUSE counts with controls, pane name, `gh auth status` in words, `core.sshCommand` path, lock-tool hash, the `brief_seat: model=...` line, target and hard stop absolute), then one line per Step 1-8 (not started / running / done / STOPPED with evidence path). **The LAST LINE of the file is, while you work, `WORKING: <step and what is running, with a figure that moves>`;** write no `READY FOR QA`, `PARTIAL:`, `STOPPED:` or `BLOCKED:` line anywhere (not even as a quotation at the start of a line) until you mean it: the coordinator's watcher reads only the last line. Heartbeat every waiter and long loop into `session-tools/b889/logs/heartbeat.txt` at least every 30 s with a MOVING figure (a load1 reading, `unit i of N`, elapsed seconds, a log size); three beats unmoved = stuck: say so. Wait on a recorded pid (`kill -0`) or a done-marker file, never `pgrep -f` from a shell whose argv holds the pattern. **RESUME at about 80 percent of context:** `WORKING: RESUME NEEDED at Step <n>` and a RESUME section (done, next command, paths, pids, commits so far).
**Sections:** Step 0 / BLUF (done or not, the head sha, the commit, the counts pair) / PINS (main, open PRs and live branches at start and before the push, the printed intersection, the blobs of the test file, `backend/jsonStorage.js` and the counts file before and after) / PRIOR WORK / DESIGN (D1-D8) / TESTED (the green table at main with the received observed objects and preconditions, the red-first baseline of G under GM6, the tamper controls, the mutant-by-test matrix with received figures beside the predicted one, `Tests:` lines baseline, after and every neighbour, the `--update-counts` output and the counts diff, the verify lines, the Step-8 runs table) / MEASURED (numstat, the two removed lines and the added lines, property regexes, gitleaks, the CodeQL pre-scan line by line) / FINDINGS (anything unexpected, at least: the line shifts against the ticket's numbers (the ticket cites main `79addb5a`; probe lines are the same at `bdb9c170`, blob `bba3742b`); `isWritable` not driven and why; the mode unpinned by design; whether any mutant outside GM6/GM11/GX2 slips through the cells) / NOT TESTED (at least: CodeQL on the new head; `Build` and `Gitleaks Scan` on the PR; the Linux runner and node 24 for each mutant; two real processes; a real full disk) / FOR THE COORDINATOR (the head is a NEW head; ONE PR; wait for every `Analyze (<language>)` run to COMPLETE; read the PR analysis for NEW alerts; both thresholds; land the SAME gated commit as a MERGE commit, never squash, never rebase; the merge starts `Build` that must read 5223 + N / 310; **land this lane BEFORE B890; if B890 added a cell and so touched the counts file, its landing resolves the conflict by C-57 regeneration with the id-superset control**) / Fixed / Deferred / Open / Corrections / Processes, ports, locks and trees left. **Last line, exactly one of:**
- `READY FOR QA: B889 NEXUSAI RD-899 WRITE PROBE CELL b889/nexusai-rd899-write-probe-cell @ <sha40, read by ls-remote AFTER your push> / tier <per the Stamp> / 1 commit on main <main sha40> (<n> ahead, <m> behind) / diff exactly the rd891 test file and the counts file / test file 2 lines removed (cell G's), backend and static numstat empty / cell J green at main, red under GM11 and GX2, cell G red under GM6, the 11 old tests green under all three / counts <5223+N> / 310 regenerated once, equal to verify / verify VERDICT PASS tests <n> suites <m> at the head / no product byte / no Deploy demo run on the branch / CodeQL UNMEASURED / 0 dismissals / 0 Jira writes / 0 gh writes / PRIOR WORK present`
