## BASE / BRANCH / IDENTITY
Code repo `/Volumes/Laptop-DEV/!CODING/Datasec/NexusAI/2_Project_Files` (shared checkout: READ verbs only, STALE), origin `datasecau/Reporting_Dashboard_Au`. Main at start is whatever `ls-remote` reads (drafter: `bdb9c170c5f6ac14cd2073e703bd719159f286a1`). Your tree: the plain clone `worktrees/b889-write-probe-cell`, branch `b889/nexusai-rd899-write-probe-cell` created at `origin/main`. Refs before/after to `session-tools/b889/logs/refs-{before,after}.txt`, equal by program (control: a dropped name is reported); the remote gains at most one ref. **Ref names:** the clone's default refspec makes `origin/b889/nexusai-rd899-write-probe-cell`; never fetch a short ref `refs/remotes/origin/b889` (a file/directory collision, the correction B865 and B870 both recorded).
**Commit identity (BY PROGRAM, never typed, never quoted):** after the Step-1 fetch, read `git --no-optional-locks log -1 --merges --format=%ae origin/main` and `--format=%an` into shell variables inside one `bash -c`; assert the email ends with `@users.noreply.github.com` (else `STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY` naming only "latest merge commit author is not a noreply address"); then commit with `git -c user.name="$N" -c user.email="$E" commit ...` (no `git config` write of an identity, no global config). After the commit assert `git log -1 --format=%ae` equals `$E` and contains no `localdomain` (control: the same assertion against a string holding `localdomain` fails). STATUS says "identity set from the latest merge commit author; verified, not quoted" and carries neither the name nor the address.
